# Service-Owned Blueprint Living SSoT Guard

For any service-owned work, first read the service file:

packages/surfaces/src/service-owned/<service>/SERVICE_BLUEPRINT.md

## Mandatory Rules

1. Each service must own a compact SERVICE_BLUEPRINT.md.
2. Do not add noisy generated screen catalogs.
3. Do not mark UI/UX/Flow, Binding, Integration, API, Runtime Vars, Guards, QA, or full closure as VERIFIED/CLOSED unless the service blueprint is updated with evidence.
4. Any service evidence must be written under kdt/volatile/registry/runs/{SESSION_ID}.
5. Unknown phase fields must remain TBD.
6. Full service closure must remain NOT CLOSED until all required phases pass evidence gates.

## Current Baseline

- DSH has a filled app-client section.
- Other service blueprints may start as TEMPLATE / TBD only.
- Future service work must progressively update the correct service blueprint.

